WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.890
The best operating system is the one that supports the hardware, runtime, and maintenance habits of the person using it.

00:00:08.890 --> 00:00:14.886
Windows is often the lowest-friction path for a shared gaming and AI machine.

00:00:14.886 --> 00:00:24.602
Driver installation is familiar, consumer applications remain available, and tools such as LM Studio or Ollama can provide a straightforward first experience.

00:00:24.602 --> 00:00:36.800
If the workstation must still function as the owner's gaming PC, preserving a stable Windows setup may be more valuable than adopting a technically elegant but unfamiliar environment.

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:42.796
Linux offers deeper control over services, scripting, permissions, containers, and many machine-learning toolchains.

00:00:42.796 --> 00:00:50.445
It is attractive for a dedicated workstation or a user comfortable diagnosing packages, drivers, and kernel interactions.

00:00:50.445 --> 00:00:53.546
That control has a maintenance cost.

00:00:53.546 --> 00:01:06.158
A Linux distribution, GPU driver, runtime, and model framework still need compatible versions, and an automatic update can disrupt a previously working stack if changes are not managed deliberately.

00:01:06.158 --> 00:01:14.221
Dual boot separates gaming and AI environments cleanly, but requires disk planning and a reboot to switch workloads.

00:01:14.221 --> 00:01:20.630
A separate AI installation on another SSD can reduce risk to the primary system.

00:01:20.630 --> 00:01:35.309
Windows Subsystem for Linux provides Linux tooling without a complete second operating system and works well for many development workflows, but GPU pass-through, networking, storage paths, and memory behavior add another layer to troubleshoot.

00:01:35.309 --> 00:01:40.064
Verify that the intended runtime officially supports the selected arrangement.

00:01:40.064 --> 00:01:44.819
Choose based on skill level and workload, then favor stability.

00:01:44.819 --> 00:01:50.814
Document driver and runtime versions, control update timing, and keep a recovery path.

00:01:50.814 --> 00:02:00.118
The operating system is not a performance trophy; it is the foundation that should make routine inference predictable, understandable, and supportable.
